invariant: INV-26
file: aes_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aes-equiv
reason: the host object's arm64 key expansion starts from the wrong round
  constant, so it computes a different key schedule from AES=soft and a
  different block from it. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof
  covers this file and bin/aes_equiv_test is the whole of what holds it:
  it runs both implementations over the same keys and blocks and compares
  the round keys and the cipher output byte for byte. The edit lands in
  the word loop only an arm64 compiler reads, so the script builds that
  binary for arm64 and for x86-64 and runs each under qemu. Without the
  equivalence test this divergence reaches a build that reads every QUIC
  Initial packet wrong and no gate says so.

--- old
static void expand(const uint8_t *key, size_t key_len, uint8_t *round_keys, size_t schedule_len) {
    uint8_t round_constant = 0x01;
--- new
static void expand(const uint8_t *key, size_t key_len, uint8_t *round_keys, size_t schedule_len) {
    uint8_t round_constant = 0x02;
